WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:07.069
. It's important to keep an eye on the things
that administrations do in the waning days

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:08.069
of a presidency.

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:11.610
Barack Obama did many things in the last days
of his presidency.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.950
George W. Bush also did.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:19.600
And one of the things that the outgoing Trump
administration did is on December 1st, they

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:26.770
rolled out their new citizenship test for
new prospective U.S. citizens.

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:28.320
Why did we need a new test?

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.570
Well, we didn't, but the Trump administration
put one in place.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:37.809
And not only is it filled with right wing
bias, it's also riddled with hilarious factual

00:00:37.809 --> 00:00:40.649
errors, legal errors, historical errors.

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:44.399
They can't do anything right in spirit, nor
by the letter.

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:50.749
So for those who aren't familiar with this
test, anyone not born a citizen needs to pass

00:00:50.749 --> 00:00:53.940
an oral test to become a citizen, to become
naturalized.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.539
20 questions, you have to pass 12.

00:00:57.539 --> 00:01:00.729
And that's a 60 percent correct answer rate.

00:01:00.729 --> 00:01:04.910
The new test is filled with questions about
most things, about things that most people

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.280
born in the U.S. citizens don't even know.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.110
Specific questions about Alexander Hamilton.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:14.660
The Trump administration has put in questions
about the Tenth Amendment, which most people

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:15.820
know nothing about.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.880
And it's clear that the idea is.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:22.210
Just make it more difficult to become a naturalized
citizen, and in order to do so, you have to

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:25.560
sort of buy into a bunch of right wing Trumpy
and propaganda.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.730
Some of them actually say these new questions
that the correct answer is something that

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:32.310
is just factually wrong.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.310
Here's an example question.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.150
Who does a U.S. senator represent?

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:42.410
The study guide say the study guide says the
correct answer is citizens of the state.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:47.990
Now, this might seem obvious, but senators
represent all people in a state.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:50.510
It includes permanent residents as an example.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:55.380
Now, this is clearly an anti-immigration type
of answer.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.130
Senators don't represent illegals.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:01.600
Now, in some ways, senators do represent undocumented
immigrants.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.800
But even without arguing that the the correct
answer can't be all citizens because permanent

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:11.840
residents here legally with green cards have
representation from senators.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:14.319
So it's it's factually wrong.

00:02:14.319 --> 00:02:17.689
Here's another wacky question from Trump's
new citizenship test.

00:02:17.689 --> 00:02:21.269
What are three rights of everyone living in
the United States?

00:02:21.269 --> 00:02:25.060
And you can choose from freedom of expression,
freedom of speech, freedom of assembly, freedom

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.880
to petition the government, freedom of religion,
the right to bear arms.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.359
Those would all be acceptable.

00:02:29.359 --> 00:02:35.319
Missing is the right to a lawyer, the right
to due process, the right to equal protection,

00:02:35.319 --> 00:02:38.310
the right to freedom from unreasonable search
and seizure.

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:40.620
Those are not listed as acceptable answers.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:45.120
The right to bear arms, which is listed, is
not absolute.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:51.709
Phelan's as an example, are limited in their
right to bear arms, but the right to due process

00:02:51.709 --> 00:02:53.340
is completely missing.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.269
It's a factual joke.

00:02:55.269 --> 00:02:56.889
And then one more for you.

00:02:56.889 --> 00:02:58.840
What is the supreme law of the land?

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:03.439
The study guide says the answer is the US
Constitution.

00:03:03.439 --> 00:03:05.440
This is utterly insane.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:12.859
The law of the land includes the Constitution,
all laws, statutes and treaties that we have,

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.209
and that's even in the Constitution.

00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:24.450
The Constitution says that the full law includes
statutes and statutes, not statutes, statutes,

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:26.230
laws and treaties.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:28.659
Trump couldn't even pass this test.

00:03:28.659 --> 00:03:30.090
Let me put it a different way.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:35.290
Even Trump couldn't pass the bogus test they've
created, even as they delineate the right

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.290
answers.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:40.569
And Trump also couldn't pass the test that
we had up until December 1st.

00:03:40.569 --> 00:03:41.879
This is really horrible.

00:03:41.879 --> 00:03:48.769
And it's sort of a it encapsulates so much
of what is wrong about the perspective that

00:03:48.769 --> 00:03:50.969
is espoused by this administration.

00:03:50.969 --> 00:03:56.400
Now, the good news is this is something that
Joe Biden should relatively quickly be able

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.499
to fix once he takes office.

00:03:59.499 --> 00:04:02.280
And I hope that he will let me know your thoughts.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.900
I'm on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:05.339
And we'll be back right after this.

